3285,"Alert - Unauthorized Use of the Online Banking
To: richard@happyday.demon.co.uk, We have been receiving complaints from our customers for unauthorized use of the Santander Online Banking. As a result we are updating our new security Modules and making an extra security check on all of our customers, in order to protect their accounts from theft and fraud. Our New banking security modules help you to better protect your online accounts than ever before. What you need to do : Log into your account here Enter your Personal ID and information (that you selected during the online enrollment process). Enter the requested verification information (including Mobile Number). However, Failure to do so may result in temporary account suspension. Please understand that this is a security measure intended to help protect you and your account. We apologize for any inconvenience. If you have any problems or questions, please call the Customers service number on the back of your Debit card. Thank you for Banking with us. Accounts Management As outlined in our User Agreement, Santander UK plc will periodically send you information about site changes and enhancements. Visit our Privacy Policy and User Agreement if you have any questions.",i04,Content Access,"GENERAL SETTINGS
